{
  "title": "61: al-Saff الصف",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nسَبَّحَ لِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ۚ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(1)\nSABBAHA LILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WA HOWA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nHalloweth God whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth; and He is the Ever-Prevalent, the All-Wise.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لِمَ تَقُوْلُوْنَ مَا لَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(2)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LEMA TAQOOLOONA MAA LAA TAF-A’LOON.\nO’ ye who believe! Why say ye what ye (yourselves) do (it) not?\nكَبُرَ مَقْتًا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ اَنْ تَقُوْلُوْا مَا لَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(3)\nKABURA MAQTAN I’NDAL LAAHE AN TAQOOLOO MAA LAA TAF-A’LOON.\nMost hateful is it unto God that ye say what ye (yourselves) do (it) not.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الَّذِيْنَ يُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِهٖ صَفًّا كَاَنَّهُمْ بُنْيَانٌ مَّرْصُوْصٌ‏(4)\nINNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL LAZEENA YOQAATELOONA FEE SABEELEH MALAAA-EKATO KA-ANNAHUM BUNYAANUN MMARSOOSUN.\nVerily God loveth those who fight in His way in ranks as if they were an unbreakable metalled wall.\nوَاِذْ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِقَوْمِهٖ يٰقَوْمِ لِمَ تُؤْذُوْنَنِىْ وَقَد تَّعْلَمُوْنَ اَنِّىْ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ اِلَيْكُمْؕ فَلَمَّا زَاغُوْۤا اَزَاغَ اللّٰهُ قُلُوْبَهُمْ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(5)\nWA IZ QAALA MOOSAA LEQAWMEHI LE-QAWMEHI LEMA TUZOONANEAA WA QAD TTAA’LAMOONA AANNEAA RASOOLAL LAAHE AELAYKUM FALAMMAA ZAAGHOOA AAZAAGHA LAAHO QULOOBAHUM WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ FAASEQEEN.\nAnd when said Moses unto his people: “O’ ye my people! Why do ye pain me? while indeed ye know that verily I am an apostle of God unto you;” but when (yet) went they astray, God (too) allowed their hearts (to astray)’, and God guideth not the people who transgress.\nوَاِذْ قَالَ عِيْسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ يٰبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اِنِّىْ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ اِلَيْكُمْ مُّصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَىَّ مِنَ التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَمُبَشِّرًۢا بِرَسُوْلٍ يَّاْتِىْ مِنْۢ بَعْدِى اسْمُهٗۤ اَحْمَدُ‌ؕ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ قَالُوْا هٰذَا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(6)\nWA IZ QAALA E’ESAB ABNU MARYAMAL YAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ INNEE RASOOLAL LAAHE ELAYKUM MMUSADDEQAN LEMAA BAYNA YADAA MENAL WA WAMUBASSHERAN BE-RASOOLIN YYAATEAA MIN BAA’DEAA FEEHAS AAHMADU FALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE QAALOO HAAZAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nAnd when said Jesus, son of Mary: “O’ ye the children of Israel! Verily I am an apostle of God unto you, confirming what is before you of the Torah and bearing (unto you) the glad tidings of an Apostle who shall come after me, his name being Ahmed (i.e. Muhammad) and when came he (Ahmed) unto them said they: “This is a manifest Sorcery!\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ وَهُوَ يُدْعٰٓى اِلَى الْاِسْلَامِ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(7)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA WA HOWA YUDA’AAA ELAL AL-AESLAAME WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd who is more unjust than he who forgeth a lie against God while he is invited unto Islam? and God guideth not the unjust people.\nيُرِيْدُوْنَ لِيُطْفِئُوْا نُوْرَ اللّٰهِ بِاَ فْوَاهِهِمْ وَاللّٰهُ مُتِمُّ نُوْرِهٖ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(8)\nYOREEDOONA LEETFEOOA NOORA LAAHE BE-AFWAAHEKUM FWAAHEHEM WAL LAAHO MUTEMMU NOOREH WA LAW KAREHA KAAFEROON.\nIntend they to put out the Light of God with their mouths! but God will perfect His Light, though averse may be the dis-believers.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَرْسَلَ رَسُوْلَهٗ بِالْهُدٰى وَدِيْنِ الْحَقِّ لِيُظْهِرَهٗ عَلَى الدِّيْنِ كُلِّهٖ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(9)\nHOWA LAZEE ARSALA RASOOLAHU BIL-HODAA WA DEENIL HAQQE LE-YUZHERAHU A’LAL DEENE KULLEH WA LAW KAREHA AL-MUSHREKOONA.\nHe it is who hath sent His Apostle (Muhammad) with the Guidance (Qur’an) and the Religion of Truth (Islam), that He may make it triumph over all the (other) religions, though averse may be the polytheists.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا هَلْ اَدُلُّكُمْ عَلٰى تِجَارَةٍ تُنْجِيْكُمْ مِّنْ عَذَابٍ اَلِيْمٍ‏(10)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO HAL ADULLOKUM A’LAA TEJAARATIN TUNJEEKUM MIN A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\nO’ ye who believe! shall I show you a merchandise which will deliver you from a painful chastisement?\nتُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَتُجَاهِدُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ بِاَمْوَالِكُمْ وَاَنْفُسِكُمْ‌ؕ ذٰلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(11)\nTUMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WATUJAAHEDOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE BE-ANWAALEKUM WA ANFOSEKUM ZAALEKUM KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\n(That) ye should believe in God and His Apostle, and strive in the way of God with your possessions and your selves; that is better for you, if ye but knew!\nيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ ذُنُوْبَكُمْ وَيُدْخِلْكُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ وَمَسٰكِنَ طَيِّبَةً فِىْ جَنّٰتِ عَدْنٍ‌ؕ ذٰلِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُۙ‏(12)\nYAGHFER LAKUM ZUNOOBAKUM WAYUDKHELKUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO WAMASAAKENA TAYBATAN FEE JANNATIN A’ADNIN ZAALEKA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nHe will forgive you your sins and admit you into gardens, neath which flow rivers and excellent abodes in the gardens of eternity; that is the supreme achievement.\nوَاُخْرٰى تُحِبُّوْنَهَا‌ ؕ نَصْرٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَفَتْحٌ قَرِيْبٌ‌ ؕ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(13)\nWA LAHU TUHEBBOONAHAA NASRUM MENAL LAAHE WAFATHUN QAREEB WA BASH-SHERIL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd another (blessing will He bestow) which ye love, (that is) the help from God, and a victory at hand; So give thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) the glad tidings unto the believers.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا كُوْنُوْۤا اَنْصَارَ اللّٰهِ كَمَا قَالَ عِيْسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ لِلْحَوٰارِيّٖنَ مَنْ اَنْصَارِىْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ‌ؕ قَالَ الْحَوٰرِيُّوْنَ نَحْنُ اَنْصَارُ اللّٰهِ‌ فَاٰمَنَتْ طَّآئِفَةٌ مِّنْۢ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَكَفَرَتْ طَّآئِفَةٌ ۚ فَاَيَّدْنَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا عَلٰى عَدُوِّهِمْ فَاَصْبَحُوْا ظٰهِرِيْنَ‏(14)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KOONOO AANSAARA LAAHE KAMAA QAALA E’ESAB ABNU MARYAMAL LIL-HAWAREENA MAN AANSAAREAA ELAL LAAH QAALA AL-HAWREEWNA NAHNO AANSAARU LAAHE FAAMANAT TAAA-EFATUM MIN BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ WAKAFARAT TAAA-EFATUM FAAYYADNAA LAZEENA AAMANOO A’LAA A’ADOOHEM FA-ASBAHOO ZAAHEREENA.\nO’ ye who believe! Be ye the helpers (in the cause) of God as said Jesus, son of Mary unto (his) disciples: “Who (among you) wall be my helpers unto (the work of) God?” Said the disciples (of Jesus) “We are the helpers (in the cause) of God! “Then believed a party of the children of Israel and disbelieved a party (among them), Then We aided those who believed against their enemy, so they became victorious",
  "merits": "Surah al-Saff (The Ranks)\nThis Surah has 14 verses and it was revealed in Madinah. It is narrated that is a person recites this Surah, as long as he remains alive, Prophet Eesaa (a.s.) seeks forgiveness from Allah (s.w.t.) for him and he will be from among the friends of Prophet Eesaa (a.s.) on the Day of Reckoning.\nImam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) has said that the person who recites this Surah will be placed in the group of angels and Prophets on the Day of Judgement. If this Surah is continually recited during a dangerous journey, the reciter is protected until he reaches his destination."
}
